WEBVTT

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.370
"Basic Lifesaving Course"
"First-Years"
"Second-Years"
"Third-Years"

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.410
We're finally done.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:14.620
--We're finally done!

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.660
--Were you able to do
mouth-to-mouth resuscitation properly?
--We're finally done!

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.370
--Were you able to do
mouth-to-mouth resuscitation properly?
--Yeah.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.750
But of course!

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.660
Apparently, I wasn't getting air in at all.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.290
I don't think I can save anyone.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.950
Yeah, you're probably
the one that'll need saving.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.620
We're supposed to practice swimming
with our clothes on for club today, right?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.950
I don't think I can do that either.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.500
We sure are learning a lot today.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.410
Oh, Ohno-<i>senpai</i>.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.830
Oh, good morning!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.080
Oh... good morning.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.910
Wh-What's wrong?

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.870
Hey, Breakwater Club!

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.040
Get over here!

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.950
Perfect timing. Meet at the pool after school.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.330
You didn't forget, right?

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.450
We remembered!

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:09.750
Especially Miss Ohno, you need to
do your best until you get it, okay?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.410
O-Okay...

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.830
Oh, right. Ohno-<i>senpai </i>can't sw--

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.200
Shh!

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.120
Senpai! I'm only able to dog paddle!
Let's both do our best together!

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.580
Okay. Thank you...

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:59.950
One, two, three, four. Two, two, three, four.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:06.370
Three, two, three, four. Four, two, three, four.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:12.200
The Breakwater Club is at high risk
of getting into water-related accidents

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.370
which could mean life or death.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.870
You all need to always be fully alert

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.790
in order to make sure you
don't get into any accidents.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.830
We will now begin our yearly
swimming lessons with our clothes on

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.950
so you remember to act calmly and

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.120
rationally even if you
were to fall into the ocean.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.540
I need the first-years and Miss Ohno
to pay especially close attention.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.120
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.830
Y-Yes, ma'am...

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.750
Ms. Sayaka seems so cool today.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.080
She seems like a PE teacher.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.200
I was a lifeguard when I was in college.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.000
I've got a certificate and everything.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.870
Wow, so you were a super active college student.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:55.000
All right. I think I'm going to have
Miss Kuroiwa show how it's done.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.160
Sure.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.410
Wow, that was easier than expected.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:02.950
Well, this involves life or death.
I'll take it seriously.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:07.620
So cold. Guess summer's still a long ways away.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.450
Upsy daisy.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.950
I know I said you'd be
swimming with your clothes on,

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.000
but you won't actually be swimming today.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.200
I'm just going to have you float like this.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.620
Being able to float like this
is extremely important.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.870
You need to not waste any energy swimming

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.580
and concentrate on just
floating until help arrives.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.830
If you fall in, don't panic.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.700
It's important to relax your body and float.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:43.950
Keep your eyes open and observe
where your balance is within the water.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.620
Lay on your back and
spread out your arms and legs.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.120
If you keep your chin up, stick out your chest,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:54.000
breathe in, and take shallow breaths,
it'll be easier to keep air in your lungs

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.620
which will help you stay afloat.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.200
Ms. Sayaka!

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.410
I'm pretty sure I can't do something
that complicated without panicking!

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.120
That's exactly why we're about to practice this.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.160
It sounds complicated when I explain it,

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.120
but doing it is a lot simpler.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.290
By the way,

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:15.410
I'm totally able to sleep in this position...

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.830
If you sleep, you'll die,
so please don't copy her.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.750
I sure won't.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.450
All right, let's have you
split into groups of two.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.250
First, let's practice floating on our backs.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:31.450
It feels weird moving around
in the pool with your tracksuit on.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.370
Ohno.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.290
Yes...

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.290
Yer heavy. Hurry and stand up.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.080
P-Please wait...

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.040
Look, yer feet can totally touch
the bottom. Ya ain't gonna drown.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.870
But, but, but...

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:51.790
Not to mention ya got two huge
flotation devices on yer chest.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.580
Ya ain't gonna drown.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.660
She sounds like an old guy.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.000
That's mean.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.910
Are you okay in the water, Hina?
You can't swim, can you?

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.250
--I can't swim, but as long as I'm somewhere
I know my feet will touch in the pool
--Hello? Earth to Ohno. Hurry up and get in.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.120
--it's not that scary.
--Hello? Earth to Ohno. Hurry up and get in.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.620
But if I can't see the bottom
like deep in the ocean, no way.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.290
Just thinking about it is scary.
The ocean's terrifying.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.750
I'm surprised you were even able to fish then.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.290
Yes, the ocean is terrifying.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.950
It's important you always remember
that in whatever you do there.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:27.250
Hup... Okay, let's do this, Hina.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.160
O-Okay...

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.950
Spread out my arms and legs,
then stick my chest out and...

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.580
Not bad at all.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.040
R-Really? Am I doing it?

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.330
Okay, me next.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.290
You're really good, Natsumi.

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:48.410
Yeah!

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:50.450
Hey, stop grabbin' onto me!

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:56.410
Miss Ohno, relax, relax!

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.790
You can even use a water
bottle as a flotation device.

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:04.540
Put some water in to act as a weight,

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.750
find the person drowning, and...

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.540
...toss it!

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:15.330
Here.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.950
If you hold it to your chest
like an otter as she's doing,

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.620
it'll make it easier to float.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.120
Tying a rope to a cooler and
throwing that in will also work.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.910
Yer crushin' it. Yer crushin' it.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.080
Ya really haven't changed much from last year.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:39.120
Ya need to get used to
the water first and foremost.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.790
Well, she has her reasons,
so we have to take our time with this.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:51.290
Actually, I've got some
excellent news for Miss Ohno.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.750
Ta-dah! We finally got them!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:56.620
An inflatable belt life jacket!

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.330
If you wear this along with
the usual life jacket you wear,

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.620
you should be fine, even if you fall in.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.870
Sure took long enough to get here.

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:09.200
I was waiting for the latest model
that's super lightweight to be released.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.410
"NEW Model"
I was waiting for the latest model
that's super lightweight to be released.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:12.910
I was waiting for the latest model
that's super lightweight to be released.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:16.290
"NEW Model"
You'd prefer that it's lightweight
and easier to move in, right?

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.080
It's so thin!

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:25.290
It's so light!

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:30.330
It doesn't feel weird. It's great.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.040
We couldn't buy them before
because of the club budget,

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:36.330
but having a life jacket on
when you're fishing is key,

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:39.000
so make sure you have these on from now on.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.620
Um, Ms. Sayaka?

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.540
Yes, Miss Tsurugi?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.120
Is it really going to
float when it's this flimsy?

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:48.120
I'll go ahead and show
you how you float with it.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:50.160
It's important to know how it works.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.410
Let me see it.

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:56.000
This life jacket is self-inflating
and when it senses water,

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:59.200
the flattened pouch
automatically fills up with air.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.660
This is what fills it up with air.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:04.160
Ah...

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:10.450
When this senses water, the CO2 in
this air tank is immediately released.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.370
This yellow part is the flotation device.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:15.540
This instantly fills up with air like, "pshhu!"

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.290
Oh...

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.660
How do I describe it...?
It's almost like an airbag in a car.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.450
Huh...

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:31.000
Hmm... I guess it's hard to
imagine without actually seeing it.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.120
I know!

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:36.750
Let's have Miss Ohno show us what it looks like.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.370
Since you can't float on your own,

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:42.000
we'll have to get you to float
properly with a life jacket on.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.660
Are you sure? Once it fills up
with air, it's pretty much done, right?

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.120
We have a replacement air tank, so it's fine.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.450
Oh, but we'll just be using
one with Miss Ohno today.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.750
All right, come on down.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:55.620
Senpai!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:56.870
You've got this!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:00.000
Don't worry. I'll be here to support you.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.540
Dive into my arms!

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:07.200
If I were to fall into the ocean...

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.580
I don't want to cause everyone trouble!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.000
Um...

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.870
You took that a bit too literally!

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.450
I-I'm floating...

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.910
Yay!

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:56.830
Yeah!

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:00.620
Ya sure are.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:02.120
That looks fun.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.500
Yeah.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.080
Right?

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.250
I thought I was a goner...

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.160
Woo-hoo!

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.080
Man, this is great.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.250
L-Let's get out now.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.910
Aw, come on. Let's stay in a little longer.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.290
Ohno-<i>senpai</i>, it's okay, relax.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:32.700
Remember when I said only
one of you can use this today?

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:36.330
I only have one replacement tank.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:37.500
"NEW Model"

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.370
"NEW Model"
"Life jacket (Belt type)"
Make sure you reimburse me for the three
tanks you wasted with your club funds.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:42.620
"Replacement Air Tank" "Easy to install!"
"Life jacket (Belt type)"
Make sure you reimburse me for the three
tanks you wasted with your club funds.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:43.160
Make sure you reimburse me for the three
tanks you wasted with your club funds.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:53.000
"Report 09"
"'Preparations and Herons'"
"Using force"

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.700
The rainy season's finally over.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.700
It's been so long since we've gone fishing.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.330
Okay, all set.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:08.120
I'm glad we got to buy the replacement
tanks. Are our funds still okay?

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.750
Somewhat.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.500
Wait, you're not going to fish today, President?

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:15.450
Yeah, pass. I'm just gonna
enjoy the nice, cool, evenin' air.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.540
Forget her. Let's go.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.250
The water's so cloudy.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.580
Well, it had been raining for a while.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:29.450
We just wanted to enjoy some fishing
with <i>burakuri </i>rigs, but we can't see a thing.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:33.410
Can the fish even see the bait?
Will we be able to fish?

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.870
It's actually easier when
the water's all murky sometimes.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.580
Really?

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:42.620
Don't worry. Fish have excellent
sight and sense of smell.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.370
Not to mention, when the water's
all cloudy like this they can't see people,

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:49.700
so they tend to let their guard
down, making them easier to catch.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.950
Even rockfish leave their nests
in search for food sometimes.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.540
I see.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.370
So we don't even have to drop into the rocks.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.290
You can just lightly cast and...

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.870
...swing your rod up and down slowly.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:11.200
While tapping on the ground to get their
attention, you just slowly pull in and...

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.450
Just like that.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:20.200
I guess this is another
way to use <i>burakuri </i>rigs.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.750
Make sure you release anything
15 centimeters and under.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.450
Okay!

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:31.700
How relaxing. It's so nice
to be able to fish again.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.000
It's a bit hot though.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:39.910
There!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.580
What do you think?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:55.330
Hm... It's 13 centimeters!

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.410
Boo, so close...

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:07.200
Wait, I'm sorry. I'll put you back.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.500
Hey!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.830
What's goin' on?

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.870
A heron stole the scorpy that Hina caught!

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:33.120
Oh, is that it? I thought
someone fell into the ocean.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:39.660
That bird's called a heron? It got
so close suddenly it scared me.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:44.660
They get close to people fishin'
in order to get their scraps.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.790
And looks like they got ya good.

00:14:47.950 --> 00:14:51.160
Right when I was trying
to return it into the ocean...

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.620
I hate that bird.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.750
They're huge and their eyes are creepy.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.830
You're not getting one from me again!

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.910
Yeah, their eyes are scary.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:04.290
Well, it ain't good to try
to tame them with food.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.500
It's best just to ignore them.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.160
Hup!

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:22.000
Oh, this one's small, too.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.660
Get bigger and let me catch you again.

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.870
You stupid bird!

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.790
You're not supposed to eat
anything smaller than 15 centimeters!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.040
You do realize you're yelling at a bird, right?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.330
They're definitely targetin' ya now.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.830
Ya need to let them go
before that bird comes around.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.370
Jeez, Hina. You're so slow.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:54.660
Well, I'm not used to getting
the hook off them yet!

00:15:56.080 --> 00:16:00.040
It's enjoying it so much... How dare you?

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:07.160
P-President Kuroiwa, its feet...

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.750
It's a fishin' line someone left behind.

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:22.120
There're idiots out there that just
throw their lines and rigs away around here.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.450
And there're plenty of animals
that get caught up in that mess.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.830
That's awful...

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:32.120
Thankfully, it just lost some toes.
Some of them end up losin' a whole foot.

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:36.620
Can't we get it off the bird somehow?

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:40.700
Well, it's a bird. Ya ain't
gonna catch it that easily.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:44.910
They can also see behind them,
so it's hard to get close.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.120
I suddenly don't feel
like fishin' anymore today.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:50.450
You weren't fishing anyway.

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:52.660
Why don't we pick up some
of the trash while we're here?

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:54.580
Yeah.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:57.410
Having clear cases like
this is really convenient.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:02.500
Let's put everything in here for now
and split up everything later.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.000
I see!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.500
There are even cases that'll wind up
leftover lines. These are also convenient.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.120
I see!

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.620
Do they sell those at Takohigeya?

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.330
Yeah, they do.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.500
Natsumi, let's go buy some on our way home.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.000
Okay!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.120
Well, guess we can call it a day.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:22.870
Okay!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:33.410
Hina!

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.370
Oh, right.

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:55.290
"Herons fishing lines"

